UID:120821-1779449400-1779451200@www.naturalsciences.org
SUMMARY:Ocean Travelers
DESCRIPTION:The Life that Lives on Floating Litter\nJoin us in the SECU Daily Planet Theater for a special presentation with renowned marine biologist Dr. Martin Thiel. \nThe large ocean currents\, like the Gulf Stream\, transport floating objects over long distances. Many different organisms attach to these floating objects. Nowadays one of the most common types of floating objects is plastic litter. In this interactive ocean adventure\, we will meet some of these ocean travelers\, and we will learn about some of the extraordinary trips they took. Just like real scientists\, we will explore where these ocean travelers are going and why we need to watch out for them. We will also learn about plastic pollution and what we all can do to keep our oceans clean. \nDr. Martin Thiel is a marine biologist with interests in invertebrate biology and the ecology of marine communities. Martin is the managing director of the Marine Global Earth Observatories (MarineGEO) network at the Smithsonian Environmental Research Center. He served as a Professor of Marine Biology at Universidad Catolica del Norte in Coquimbo\, Chile\, for 25 years. He has studied diverse coastal ecosystems over more than 3000 miles between the dry Atacama desert and the wet Patagonian fjords.
URL:https://www.naturalsciences.org/calendar/event/ocean-travelers/
LOCATION:Nature Research Center\, 121 West Jones Street\, Raleigh\, NC\, 27601\, United States
CATEGORIES:All Ages,General Events,Lectures,Meet the Scientist,SECU Daily Planet Theater,Walk-up Programs
ORGANIZER;CN="Chris%20Smith":MAILTO:christopher.smith@naturalsciences.org
GEO:35.7822405;-78.6409677
X-APPLE-STRUCTURED-LOCATION;VALUE=URI;X-ADDRESS=Nature Research Center 121 West Jones Street Raleigh NC 27601 United States;X-APPLE-RADIUS=500;X-TITLE=121 West Jones Street:geo:-78.6409677,35.7822405
END:VEVENT
