SUMMARY:Biodiversity After Dark
DESCRIPTION:What wildlife can you see at night?  Join us at Prairie Ridge to find out!  We’ll have light stations to attract moths and other nocturnal insects\, walk to our pond to listen for frogs\, and listen for owls.  Bring a flashlight and a smartphone or camera to document the things you see! \nThis program starts at 8:30pm and will include a brief introduction to nocturnal animals before we visit our frog and insect stations.  You are welcome to leave anytime\, but we’ll keep the lights on until 11:30pm if you’d like to stay for the best chance of seeing big moths! \nRegister
URL:https://www.naturalsciences.org/calendar/event/nighttime-biodiversity/
LOCATION:Prairie Ridge\, 1671 Gold Star Drive\, Raleigh\, NC\, 27607\, United States
CATEGORIES:Adults,Children,Citizen Science,K-12 Students,Outdoor Experiences,Teens
ORGANIZER;CN="Chris%20Goforth":MAILTO:chris.goforth@naturalsciences.org
