SUMMARY:Native Plants for Birds
DESCRIPTION:Join staff from the Library of North Carolina’s Government and Heritage Library and the NC Museum of Natural Sciences for a Native Plant Walk focusing on gardening with native plants to attract and support birds (and their foodweb). \nThis plant walk will explore native plantings in the NC Department of Natural and Cultural Resources’ Native Plant Meadow and the NC Museum of Natural Science’s Native Plant Garden. The event will take place primarily outdoors\, with participants traveling approximately ½ mile round-trip via paved sidewalks. \nRegistration is requested. \nThis event is hosted in connection with the GHL’s Native Plant Seed Library. Learn more about our seed library at slnc.info/seeds\, and more about seed libraries and native plants on our GHL Seed Library Research Guide at slnc.info/seedlibraryguide. \nQuestions about this event? Contact us at ghl.info@dncr.nc.gov.
URL:https://www.naturalsciences.org/calendar/event/native-plants-for-birds/
LOCATION:Archives\, History\, & State Library Building\, 109 East Jones\, Raleigh\, North Carolina\, 27601
CATEGORIES:All Ages,Outdoor Experiences
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/png:https://www.naturalsciences.org/calendar/wp-content/uploads/2026/05/Untitled.png
END:VEVENT
